 I just have the title, so sorry.

01:33:19.740 --> 01:33:20.340
 Oh, sorry.

01:33:20.440 --> 01:33:21.960
 The phone, I don't have questions.

01:33:22.100 --> 01:33:22.280
 Okay.

01:33:23.360 --> 01:33:25.860
 It was on the, I think it was on the credit card.

01:33:27.560 --> 01:33:28.600
 So we're good on that one?

01:33:28.860 --> 01:33:29.840
 What's your credit card question?

01:33:32.360 --> 01:33:40.340
 So these are the two items that came to the council's discussion at the last meeting that we reviewed, and then this is to ratify it with the change.

01:33:41.100 --> 01:33:43.940
 So, yeah, we've talked about this, and it should have been.

01:33:43.940 --> 01:33:44.500
 Oh, okay.

01:33:44.940 --> 01:33:45.880
 My only, sorry.

01:33:46.260 --> 01:33:53.140
 I'm going through my notes, and my question was regarding the reconciliations.

01:33:53.140 --> 01:34:05.660
 It just, I think in section D5, it said review the first week, and I just wondered if maybe like having a, the seventh calendar day of the month, or something like having a specific day of the month.

01:34:05.980 --> 01:34:09.880
 So, it, it says just the first week, right?

01:34:10.020 --> 01:34:18.140
 So, for us, when we're talking about the first week, it's because there are times where our close date changes on the credit card statements.

01:34:18.140 --> 01:34:18.460
 Okay.

01:34:18.460 --> 01:34:23.100
 They have to review and have all their transactions coded within the first week of when the statement closes.

01:34:23.480 --> 01:34:25.380
 They don't have to wait that long at all.

01:34:25.840 --> 01:34:29.840
 You can, as soon as you've made a purchase, you have the ability to code and upload it.

01:34:30.340 --> 01:34:36.180
 And so, that particular item is more of an internal, like, process about the timeline that we want them to be able to do it.

01:34:36.180 --> 01:34:43.420
 But we'd rather not have it say, like, by the fifth day of the month, because sometimes that statement date changes.

01:34:43.720 --> 01:34:44.540
 It changes. Okay. Thank you.

01:34:48.460 --> 01:34:50.580
 You didn't have any questions.

