 All right.

01:34:50.980 --> 01:34:58.680
 13F was a resolution of Eagle Mountain City approving a contract with MHTN Architects for the City Hall and Library Feasibility Study.

01:35:00.320 --> 01:35:00.720
 Yeah.

01:35:00.720 --> 01:35:09.840
 The comment I wanted to make on this one, I just feel like that we've put a lot of effort and time and wanted a lot more input into how downtown is.

01:35:09.840 --> 01:35:21.140
 And I would like this to have two council members that are part of that decision-making body, rather than us wait until the decisions are made and then say no.

01:35:23.060 --> 01:35:26.100
 That's my opinion, if anybody else agrees with that.

01:35:26.520 --> 01:35:32.360
 And, Mayor, real quick, we do have Ryan Wallace on from MHTN to answer any questions as well.

01:35:32.700 --> 01:35:33.980
 He won't be shocked by that.

01:35:34.480 --> 01:35:45.540
 We can't hear you, Ryan, but I did warn him that that's probably what the council will want, is more involvement, which is a good thing.

01:35:46.420 --> 01:35:50.660
 And I can attest that they're really great at working with council members because...

01:35:50.660 --> 01:35:51.720
 Because we broke them in.

01:35:51.860 --> 01:35:56.640
 Well, no, council member Curtis and I worked with them on the Smith Ranch Park.

01:35:56.640 --> 01:36:02.340
 And, like, so I feel like they're great at taking the feedback and pulling us in, so.

01:36:05.200 --> 01:36:10.480
 So I think this is going to approve a contract that will allow them to start work.

01:36:10.620 --> 01:36:20.120
 I think we're going to have to have some working groups because I know that I've been, that council members have reached out more than two that want to be involved in this.

01:36:20.120 --> 01:36:27.500
 So we're going to have to go two by two or, you know, mayor and council at some point in time as this goes.

01:36:27.740 --> 01:36:33.840
 There's going to be a ton of discussion on building height and design and architectural aspects.

01:36:34.000 --> 01:36:40.200
 So I do think that Ryan and I in St. George, did it, was it?

01:36:40.460 --> 01:36:47.260
 Okay, and Craig went to dinner in St. George and had lots of discussions about different architectural things.

01:36:47.380 --> 01:36:55.340
 So we can get together two by two and work through this one, I think, without...

01:36:55.340 --> 01:36:58.680
 Why not just bring them in and let's do a meeting with all of us like they did before?

01:36:58.680 --> 01:36:59.320
 Or notice it.

01:36:59.440 --> 01:37:07.220
 And I think to start with, if Ryan's open to that, we'd almost have to because I know everybody wants to weigh in on where this goes.

01:37:07.580 --> 01:37:09.560
 So I didn't hear that.

01:37:09.640 --> 01:37:09.980
 I'm sorry.

01:37:10.460 --> 01:37:12.000
 That we should just notice a meeting.

01:37:12.820 --> 01:37:18.960
 Have a kind of a kickoff meeting with the council or I know in the proposal he talks about two meetings with the council.

01:37:18.960 --> 01:37:25.760
 I know he's probably going to want to be more involvement, but we can do it towards the beginning.

01:37:25.840 --> 01:37:32.860
 We can work with Ryan, but towards the beginning and then at certain stages where it's appropriate.

01:37:33.380 --> 01:37:33.620
 Yeah.

01:37:33.780 --> 01:37:44.940
 So if this gets approved, Ryan, maybe work with staff to pick a date or Ben, sooner rather than later, let's have a working group on this one.

01:37:45.000 --> 01:37:46.300
 Maybe we could meet an hour early.

01:37:46.300 --> 01:37:54.540
 I don't know if that fits the schedule on a Tuesday just for this and then go into our work session on a regular council day if that works.

01:37:54.600 --> 01:37:55.660
 So we'll work on that.

01:37:56.340 --> 01:37:56.800
 All right.

01:37:57.440 --> 01:38:00.180
 Is there any other questions on that one as far as the contract itself?

01:38:02.420 --> 01:38:02.780
 Okay.

01:38:02.880 --> 01:38:05.180
 Thanks for hanging with us, Ryan, for all of that.

01:38:08.080 --> 01:38:12.020
 I mean, I just want to make sure because the contract does state what we just talked about.

01:38:12.320 --> 01:38:18.440
 So who they are meeting with and how often they're meeting with, that part needs to be clear.

01:38:18.920 --> 01:38:22.420
 That it starts with the city council, there'll be a meeting in between and one at the end.

01:38:23.860 --> 01:38:25.520
 I don't think it says that right now.

01:38:28.380 --> 01:38:38.400
 So could we just say in the motion, updating the contract as discussed with the meeting, expectations with the council?

01:38:38.860 --> 01:38:39.660
 Something like that?

01:38:43.440 --> 01:38:44.600
 Yeah, something like that.

01:38:44.680 --> 01:38:52.940
 Right now it says in workshop five, which is the last step, it talks about two rounds of, no, that's the city review, sorry.

01:38:53.380 --> 01:38:57.980
 Somewhere it talks about city council up to two meetings.

01:38:58.260 --> 01:39:00.860
 But yeah, just, I think that makes sense.

01:39:00.920 --> 01:39:03.160
 What Melissa said, council member Clark.

01:39:05.980 --> 01:39:06.380
 Okay.

01:39:07.360 --> 01:39:08.160
 Moving on.

01:39:08.580 --> 01:39:10.020
 We have just a few more minutes.

01:39:10.080 --> 01:39:16.940
 And I do know I have a question here in a second, but 14A is an ordinance of Eagle Mountain City amending the youth council code 245.

01:39:17.040 --> 01:39:17.240
 Is there?

01:39:17.560 --> 01:39:19.080
 I have one question about that.

01:39:19.080 --> 01:39:19.400
 Okay.

01:39:19.720 --> 01:39:24.400
 And this is Natalie 2.45.040 duties.

01:39:24.920 --> 01:39:30.260
 And it's actually in B, limitations of the city council authority, or youth city council authority.

01:39:30.260 --> 01:39:37.060
 And we're striking number one, which says the youth city council must have a quorum in order to conduct business.

01:39:37.200 --> 01:39:39.120
 I'm curious why we're removing that.

01:39:40.220 --> 01:39:45.040
 It comes down to basically whoever shows up to the meeting will have a right to vote.

01:39:45.280 --> 01:39:53.940
 And we were concerned if, so we weren't going to limit it to only, say, five youth to being on the city council as voting members.

01:39:54.260 --> 01:40:02.580
 And the youth city council, along with advisors, recommended that whichever youth decides they want to join the city council can be a voting member.

01:40:03.180 --> 01:40:07.260
 And so we just didn't want to have to track, okay, so let's say that there's 15 of them.

01:40:07.360 --> 01:40:11.140
 Do we need seven, or do we need eight of them to have a quorum at this point?

01:40:11.520 --> 01:40:16.580
 And so the way that the code is now changed is whoever shows up is the one that wants to get a vote.

01:40:17.040 --> 01:40:20.220
 And the mayor will make a tie if there's an even number.

01:40:20.880 --> 01:40:22.920
 So that's why they modified that.

01:40:27.260 --> 01:40:30.160
 I guess I have some consternation about that.

01:40:30.500 --> 01:40:38.100
 It would be difficult for me if we decided to suspend the quorum of the city council as a decision-making body.

01:40:38.300 --> 01:40:43.980
 And yet we've got the youth council that we're trying to teach and train so they understand the way that government works.

01:40:44.700 --> 01:40:46.380
 And we're saying that there's no need for a quorum.

01:40:46.680 --> 01:40:49.360
 That's concerning to me on several levels.

01:40:50.840 --> 01:40:56.560
 I understand, Council Member Whiting, where you're coming from, that there's a big group, and are you going to have to count and keep track?

01:40:57.240 --> 01:41:05.360
 But if they're going to make decisions about where the youth council is going to do and pass motions and learn how to actually function as a council,

01:41:06.140 --> 01:41:10.020
 I find it problematic to remove the need to have a quorum present.

01:41:10.700 --> 01:41:14.760
 In theory, the mayor or the mayor and one council member could call a meeting.

01:41:15.700 --> 01:41:20.080
 Nobody else comes, and they could be making decisions that you don't want to see happen.

01:41:20.380 --> 01:41:21.720
 So the meetings have to be noticed.

01:41:22.180 --> 01:41:25.040
 But what if we did, okay, so there are a couple ways to resolve this.

01:41:25.540 --> 01:41:32.000
 One way would be, okay, a majority, a majority have to attend, or we could say simply, like a minimum number,

01:41:32.100 --> 01:41:34.260
 like there have to be at least five youth present.

01:41:34.260 --> 01:41:39.020
 I think that would feel better to me, is that there has to be at least a minimum, and that would constitute a quorum.

01:41:39.020 --> 01:41:41.160
 Okay, then let's, okay.

01:41:41.520 --> 01:41:42.980
 And I don't know what that number looks like.

01:41:43.500 --> 01:41:46.340
 It probably, that's a good question.

01:41:46.440 --> 01:41:47.600
 I mean, we've been consistent.

01:41:47.800 --> 01:41:50.440
 I mean, fortunately, we have more people that have applied this year.

01:41:50.620 --> 01:41:50.940
 That's awesome.

01:41:51.080 --> 01:41:51.700
 Which is good.

01:41:51.760 --> 01:41:55.800
 It's probably almost double the number than we normally have, which is a healthy thing.

01:41:56.280 --> 01:42:01.460
 So maybe it's easy in the quorum section to just identify we need at least, I don't know.

01:42:01.460 --> 01:42:05.880
 The quorum shall be constituted with a minimum of at least five members present, something like that.

01:42:05.880 --> 01:42:06.100
 Yeah, five.

01:42:06.200 --> 01:42:10.800
 And if they don't have five, then they can't move forward with voting on something.

01:42:12.320 --> 01:42:14.140
 Do we all feel comfortable with the number five?

01:42:14.840 --> 01:42:15.680
 Okay, I'll make the changes.

01:42:16.580 --> 01:42:18.040
 Council Member Whiting's good with that.

01:42:18.080 --> 01:42:18.600
 I'm good with that.

01:42:18.640 --> 01:42:19.660
 That was the only concern I had.

01:42:22.800 --> 01:42:27.140
 And the intent behind that, too, is, I mean, they wanted to remove seventh graders.

01:42:27.560 --> 01:42:30.760
 They wanted any youth that joined to be able to have a vote.

01:42:31.840 --> 01:42:34.800
 And so we simplified some of the language in there.

01:42:36.140 --> 01:42:39.180
 I think if you want participation, they want to feel like they have a say in it.

01:42:39.220 --> 01:42:39.980
 Otherwise, why come?

01:42:40.200 --> 01:42:40.400
 Right.

01:42:40.560 --> 01:42:40.680
 Right.

01:42:40.900 --> 01:42:41.800
 I was going to say that.

01:42:41.860 --> 01:42:45.100
 I kind of lean towards the body.

01:42:45.520 --> 01:42:48.240
 But at the same token, if you do that, you're always going to have five kids because the rest

01:42:48.240 --> 01:42:49.560
 are just feel like they're tagging along.

01:42:50.040 --> 01:42:51.700
 If you do this, everybody's involved.

01:42:51.780 --> 01:42:53.840
 It's the only real way that you can grow a program, I think.

01:42:54.020 --> 01:42:56.220
 And it makes everybody feel like they're part of it.

01:42:57.100 --> 01:43:01.580
 And they don't, they're really not making decisions that affect anyone but what they do

01:43:01.580 --> 01:43:02.660
 or whatever, so.

01:43:03.800 --> 01:43:06.740
 The next one is, no more questions on that, right?

01:43:07.120 --> 01:43:07.540
 Did you clear?

01:43:08.700 --> 01:43:12.980
 15A, a discussion about the traffic impact study of Silver Lake Parkway connection to

01:43:12.980 --> 01:43:13.760
 Saratoga Springs.

01:43:14.500 --> 01:43:20.880
 Now, I have a question on this one, only because it's been brought to my attention in other

01:43:20.880 --> 01:43:27.120
 meetings, and I don't care how this is handled, but I've heard there's going to be some people

01:43:27.120 --> 01:43:28.140
 here to discuss this.

01:43:28.700 --> 01:43:32.140
 Do you want public comment during the item or before?

01:43:32.240 --> 01:43:35.080
 It is not a public hearing.

01:43:35.240 --> 01:43:39.920
 That's why I'm asking, am I instructed to get public comment only in the public comment

01:43:39.920 --> 01:43:45.300
 period, or because this discussion is what it is, do you want the public comment to be

01:43:45.300 --> 01:43:47.240
 during the, as the discussion happens?

01:43:47.280 --> 01:43:47.860
 That's all I'm asking.

01:43:48.520 --> 01:43:49.920
 Can I just make a comment?

01:43:49.920 --> 01:43:56.540
 I think my preference would be to have the presentation, have the council discuss.

01:43:57.740 --> 01:44:05.560
 I think when we bring public comment in, if they want to comment during the opening public comment, great, but when we bring the level of emotion

01:44:05.560 --> 01:44:09.820
 in, with the presentation, it really clouds my judgment.

01:44:11.040 --> 01:44:12.380
 That's just my own preference.

01:44:12.840 --> 01:44:14.280
 I don't know if council members feel differently.

01:44:14.700 --> 01:44:17.700
 So I'd have them, if they want to make a public comment, do it at the beginning.

01:44:18.020 --> 01:44:19.320
 So keep it in the public comment section.

01:44:19.320 --> 01:44:24.540
 Keep it where it is, and then separate that from when we have the discussion on, if they want to stay and listen.

01:44:24.540 --> 01:44:25.500
 I 100% agree with that.

01:44:25.940 --> 01:44:30.260
 Because it is not a public hearing, I was just asked, are we going to allow a comment in this session?

01:44:30.260 --> 01:44:33.640
 No, I think we just follow the law and we conduct the meeting in the way that we normally would.

01:44:33.840 --> 01:44:42.040
 We've received a lot of public comment, at least I have, and I'm sure that each of you have, and that's valuable, and I value that.

01:44:42.100 --> 01:44:45.400
 But there will also be another opportunity when this comes back for adoption.

01:44:46.520 --> 01:44:49.200
 My assumption is it will be a public hearing at that point in time.

01:44:49.680 --> 01:44:50.980
 Can anybody answer that for me?

01:44:54.080 --> 01:44:54.740
 Where's David?

01:44:54.740 --> 01:44:58.560
 Marcus, this comes out as a public item when we take an action on it, right?

01:44:58.680 --> 01:45:04.720
 When the action item comes on the actual impact study, that would not be a public hearing.

01:45:04.820 --> 01:45:11.360
 No, but if we decide to adopt something to go ahead and allocate funds towards this.

01:45:11.580 --> 01:45:20.560
 Yes, when you implement, if you implement any of the plans from the study, such as improvement to intersections and things like that,

01:45:20.640 --> 01:45:26.760
 that will be a budget decision for which you will be able to formally adopt that as a council.

01:45:27.320 --> 01:45:37.160
 Yes, when you're amending a budget, for example, or adding it to the budget, there's a public hearing associated with that if it's not currently budgeted for.

01:45:37.160 --> 01:45:42.580
 And I want to be clear, I'm not saying that we shouldn't receive public hearing or public comment.

01:45:42.780 --> 01:45:49.360
 That is available every Tuesday night that we meet, and we're willing to entertain any and all of that.

01:45:49.440 --> 01:45:56.640
 But I think that to continue to make exceptions for each of these items, I just think that's a practice that we should discontinue.

01:45:56.780 --> 01:45:59.840
 Yeah, I think the only time there will be a public hearing is during a budget.

01:46:01.840 --> 01:46:08.520
 I think we need to make sure that we're intentional in letting them have an opportunity to speak about this when it comes back as an action item.

01:46:09.280 --> 01:46:16.160
 They need to have the ability to express how they feel about it, for or against it, and everybody ought to get a chance to get it out.

01:46:16.760 --> 01:46:22.080
 That way there's no question in anybody's mind that they didn't have a chance to give public comment on it.

01:46:22.900 --> 01:46:24.060
 Yeah, and I'm okay with it.

01:46:24.060 --> 01:46:24.720
 I don't really care.

01:46:24.780 --> 01:46:25.980
 I just asked the question.

01:46:26.380 --> 01:46:32.560
 But real quick, I just want to say one of the reasons why I considered it is I think if they heard the discussion of the council,

01:46:32.840 --> 01:46:38.280
 we might save ourselves 30 or 40 minutes in public comment because they might see where the council is leaning,

01:46:38.860 --> 01:46:40.820
 and that could save a lot of time.

01:46:40.880 --> 01:46:42.200
 Otherwise, we just got to listen to everybody.

01:46:42.440 --> 01:46:48.420
 So I thought, well, that could be beneficial, but I agree with just staying where we do.

01:46:50.180 --> 01:46:52.740
 I was just going to say there will be people here.

01:46:52.880 --> 01:46:57.240
 Maybe let them know if they're here to make a public comment to do it at the beginning of the meeting.

01:46:57.240 --> 01:46:58.060
 That's why I was asking.

01:46:58.480 --> 01:46:59.600
 That's what I wanted to know.

01:47:00.880 --> 01:47:04.320
 Be intentional, though, and also let them know we're not taking action today.

01:47:04.860 --> 01:47:10.960
 So if they want to give a public comment, it might be good for them to hear what the traffic study discussion and all that is,

01:47:10.960 --> 01:47:15.120
 and then they'll have an opportunity to come back and give their feedback when we take action.

01:47:16.100 --> 01:47:19.900
 That way it at least gives them a chance to understand what we're discussing.

01:47:20.980 --> 01:47:21.880
 That's just a thought.

01:47:22.680 --> 01:47:22.880
 Right.

01:47:25.800 --> 01:47:27.540
