01:49:21.620 --> 01:49:28.440
 And then 17C is the resolution adopting the fiscal year interim budget and the proposed certified tax rate.

01:49:31.120 --> 01:49:33.780
 Anything on that one that we can sort out?

01:49:33.780 --> 01:49:41.480
 Okay, and then the last one, 18A, is Ordinance of Eagle Mountain City, Utah, amending the Eagle Mountain Municipal Code 1615 on concept plans.

01:49:41.560 --> 01:49:44.960
 And I know Brandon Larson had some information on this one.

01:49:47.940 --> 01:49:50.480
 Yeah, I can talk through that a little bit.

01:49:52.360 --> 01:50:00.080
 This one, essentially what we're trying to do here is just trying to improve our development process a little bit.

01:50:00.080 --> 01:50:24.860
 So one of the things that we're trying to focus on is trying to look for, trying to make sure that right at the front of our development process that we are looking to make, looking and ensuring that we're making connections for utilities and utilities and roads.

01:50:24.860 --> 01:50:37.700
 And so the big thing here is, I guess a couple of things is just requiring some additional documents or clarifying some of the documents that we are already are requiring.

01:50:39.640 --> 01:50:53.080
 Essentially asking that the developers to give us some information to show that, you know, for instance, one of those documents is supposed to show how they're going to connect with the road system within 500 feet of their proposed development.

01:50:54.840 --> 01:51:07.860
 The other thing, too, got some feedback from a council member that maybe it might be good to be a little more judicious on how many concept plans we bring to you.

01:51:08.000 --> 01:51:34.860
 So the proposal is to generally try to take concept plans and have them end at the planning commission unless there's, I mean, there's still an ability for us to bring them on, but generally have them end at planning commission and then just take them on to council on a case-by-case basis if it's necessary.

01:51:34.860 --> 01:51:59.500
 So, but anyway, that's kind of in a nutshell what the proposal is, and then I guess the other big thing is that the concept plan would be, is typically been a, it hasn't been required, but it would be required for master developments, preliminary plats, and re-zones.

01:51:59.500 --> 01:52:14.860
 So, the one comment I have on this one, I just, thinking back in the last 12 months of when we've had them come forward to us, I think the most important thing for me is to show the full traffic circulation plan.

01:52:15.440 --> 01:52:22.560
 So, if they're, even if they're bringing phase one in, if this project has six phases, all six phases, circulation needs to be shown.

01:52:22.860 --> 01:52:23.040
 Yeah.

01:52:23.140 --> 01:52:35.960
 Because that's really what matters at that phase so that we aren't running into, basically, they're just putting in a stub here and it's going to cut off the rest of the project or adjoining properties, et cetera.

01:52:35.960 --> 01:52:45.240
 So, to me, that would be a useful purpose of the concept plan, is to be able to see what the traffic circulation plan is.

01:52:46.220 --> 01:52:46.700
 Right.

01:52:47.700 --> 01:53:00.260
 And frankly, the infrastructure, the utility infrastructure planning for me, I mean, having spent some time recently at the conference in Habert regarding water, and just spending a little more time with our public works department,

01:53:01.320 --> 01:53:13.720
 we really need to do, be more effective is probably the way I would put it in our initial review of any conceptual plan as to how we're going to service that.

01:53:13.720 --> 01:53:17.060
 And what are going to be the impacts to the system overall?

01:53:17.420 --> 01:53:26.380
 Do we have the capacity and the capability of servicing it in a way that is meaningful, or are there going to have to be some additional steps that are taken to be able to service it?

01:53:26.440 --> 01:53:32.320
 And then the demonstration that there's actually water that can support any plan that might work its way through the system.

01:53:32.480 --> 01:53:34.140
 So, I like this.

01:53:34.220 --> 01:53:34.840
